about 400 of china's most powerful  officials are meeting this week in  beijing  the secretive gathering known as the  plenum is the most important in the  country's political calendar and lays  the groundwork for the coming year  but this week's event is especially  significant  a historical resolution is due to be  unveiled this will determine the  direction of chinese politics both  philosophical and practical for years to  come it's this integration between  philosophy history and politics i think  that makes it unique and this i think is  really focusing global attention on this  new paradigm this  new  way of governing that could lead to real  breakthroughs for humanity  only three official historical  resolutions have been announced since  the chinese communist party was founded  in 1945 party founder mao zedong used  the first to claim his position as  china's absolute leader as well as point  out the missteps of early communist  revolutionaries  in 1981 a resolution announced under  deng xiaoping criticized the problems of  the cultural revolution and justified  economic and industrial reforms  this year the party will mark the  achievements of the past 100 years  it will focus on strengthening the  communist party as the only political  force in china and consolidating xi's  position as the ultimate people's leader  she's positioned in the party is now  unchallenged this is thanks to the  constant purchase during the past nine  years anti-corruption campaigns and  increasing purchase of civil society  public opinion and the internet  in 2018 beijing scrapped presidential  term limits allowing xi to rule for life  earlier this year as the communist party  celebrated a century in rule he declared  the achievement of a moderately  prosperous society  state media touted his success in  following through on promises to make  china wealthy and powerful president xi  jinping is expected to use this year's  plenum to elevate himself above previous  leaders it's likely that his version of  recent history will be accepted as the  official history of the party and he  will further strengthen his power base  but critics say there's great danger in  this  we are seeing a resurgence of  authoritarianism  one that combines the soviet ideology  nazi germany and even previous japanese  and italian models  along with china's own traditions  this means that in face of criticism  from all over the world it is very  difficult for it to react flexibly to  react with a real openness this  seclusion i believe it is the greatest  threat to the chinese communist system  now  the four-day gathering will also include  discussions on who will replace other  top leaders including the premier  starting next year  katrina u al jazeera beijing
 

